 > Any ideas re correct syntax ?...

ODS2 device name under unix is the trailing part of the unix device
path.  I.e. if it's /dev/sda, you "mount sda:".

Copy is "copy <ods2filename> <unixhostfilename>".  You can do
wildcards, like "copy ada043.* ada043.*".

Note that ods2 has an endianness issue on some archs.  I had to patch
it for x86 linux.

De


